},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/images/spacer.gif","alt":" ","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":1,"renderedHeight":10,"naturalWidth":10,"naturalHeight":10,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"DECORATIVE","altReason":"alt=\"\" (decorative)","bytes":821},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/figures/m833a2f1.gif","alt":"The figure shows consultation rates per 100,000 patient population for influenza-like illness (ILI), by health district, from the sentinel general practitioner surveillance system for New Zealand from July 6-12, 2009. During July 6-12, a week of high influenza activity, multiple health districts reported >400 ILI consultations per 100,000 patient population, which is indicative of epidemic activity. Among those health districts with epidemic activity, South Auckland had the highest consultation rate (1,308 per 100,000), followed by Wellington (709), and South Canterbury (505).","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":510,"renderedHeight":597,"naturalWidth":510,"naturalHeight":597,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 583 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":23479},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/figures/m833a2f2.gif","alt":"The figure shows national consultation rates for influenza-like illness (ILI) compared with 2008 and 2007, by week, from the sentinel general practitioner surveillance system for New Zealand, for the period from the week ending May 3 through the week ending August 2, 2009. Weekly national ILI consultation rates for the study period were compared with the same period in 2008 and 2007. From the week ending May 3 through the week ending June 7, the weekly ILI consultation rate remained below the baseline level of 50 consultations per 100,000 patient population.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":515,"renderedHeight":317,"naturalWidth":515,"naturalHeight":317,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 564 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":11615},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/figures/m833a2f3.gif","alt":"The figure shows the number of influenza viruses identified by two surveillance systems, by type, in New Zealand for the period from the week ending May 3 through week ending August 2, 2009. For the general practitioner sentinel surveillance system, the predominant strain was 2009 pandemic influenza A (H1N1) (332 [63%]), followed by seasonal influenza A (72 [14%]), seasonal influenza A (H1N1) (70[13%]), influenza A not subtyped (44 [8%]), seasonal influenza A (H3N2) (8), and influenza B not typed. For the nonsentinel laboratory surveillance network, the strain was 2009 pandemic influenza A (H1N1) (2,116), followed by influenza A (not subtyped) (1,076), seasonal influenza A (H1N1) virus (444), seasonal influenza A virus (244), seasonal influenza A (H3N2) virus (49), and influenza B (not typed) (2). ","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":423,"renderedHeight":620,"naturalWidth":423,"naturalHeight":620,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 808 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":19228},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/images/spacer.gif","alt":" ","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":10,"renderedHeight":1,"naturalWidth":10,"naturalHeight":10,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"DECORATIVE","altReason":"alt=\"\" (decorative)","bytes":821},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/headers_footers/images/spacer1.gif","alt":"","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":true,"isMissingAlt":false